ThreeFPolicy
├── configuration
│   ├── only the owner changes the consumer, budget, and minimum yield
│   ├── repointing or disabling the consumer preserves spent assets
│   ├── budget and duration changes carry active-period usage forward
│   └── minimum-yield changes apply immediately without resetting usage
├── consume
│   ├── only the current consumer can charge a configured asset
│   ├── rejects zero principal, insufficient yield, and multiplication overflow
│   ├── keeps asset budgets independent and rounds minimum yield conservatively
│   └── resets expired usage without accumulating unused capacity
├── multicall
│   ├── preserves owner authorization during configuration
│   └── preserves the consumer and rolls back all charges when the budget is exceeded
├── factory lifecycle
│   ├── initializes owner, factory, version, and consumer exactly once
│   ├── migration requires the factory and owner
│   └── migration preserves consumer, minimum yield, and active budget usage
└── isolated deterministic gas snapshots
    ├── configure and disable the consumer and minimum yield
    ├── initialize a budget, update its duration, disable, and reenable
    ├── consume first use, subsequent use, and period rollover
    ├── reject unauthorized consumption, insufficient yield, and exhausted budget
    ├── read current, disabled, and expired capacity
    └── configure through multicall
